+# UNLAUNCHED six-case exact series pilot
+
+One stdlib worker, six fixed ordered cases in pilot.py; no retries/replacements. Total prospective30s including startup, pins, arithmetic, serialization and teardown; sampled whole tree384MiB, root kill29.5s. Root verified-byte dispatcher/runtime closure and independent review/preregistration must precede evaluate(). This source freeze is not launch authority.
+
+All m values are computed from exact geometric majorants before summing coefficients and recorded in TOY_RESULT. Each row saves both rational endpoints, widths, term count and elapsed time. Completed rows and every16-term progress survive failure. No floats enter the scientific enclosure; times alone are floating. No Gram, alpha or small-s-uniform performance claim.
+
+Only preparation run: exact finite combinatorial identity versus independent factorial multinomial count through n8; weighted-geometric-tail checks; prospective m planning. These do not evaluate A or A' at a physical s. Existing coarse integral and frozen tensor-Gauss sources remain unchanged. A successful cost attempt would still require independent exact receipt/series replay before downstream numerical use.
+
+Strict dispatcher run.py now binds the exact interpreter and broad existing stdlib/dylib closure, rejects local executable/directory membership changes, compiles verified source bytes and checks actual loaded module origins before and after. Readiness executes the real parser and module initialization only. The secondary worker alarm begins after startup; root startup-inclusive29.5s watchdog remains required. Original ea6f source is preserved in sibling native-green-return-series-before-dispatch-ea6f.
+
+Every16-term progress receipt includes actual rational partial A and negative derivative sums plus rigorous remaining tails and full enclosures at that completed term count. Timeout therefore preserves useful current-case mathematical work. This narrow retention amendment preserves 08bf in a sibling folder.
